      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/36/5325",
      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ مُسْلِمٍ كَانَ فِي أَرْضِ اَلشِّرْكِ فَقَتَلَهُ اَلْمُسْلِمُونَ ثُمَّ عَلِمَ بِهِ اَلْإِمَامُ بَعْدُ فَقَالَ \"يُعْتِقُ مَكَانَهُ رَقَبَةً مُؤْمِنَةً وَ ذَلِكَ قَوْلُ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ۝ فَإِنْ كٰانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَكُمْ وَ هُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ ۝ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5325 - Ibn Abi Umayr narrated from some of his companions from Abu Abdullah (as) regarding a Muslim man who was in the land of the disbelievers and was mistakenly killed by the Muslims. Later, the Imam became aware of it.\nImam (as) said: \"A believing slave must be freed in his place, and this is in accordance with the saying of Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic:\n'But if he belonged to a people hostile to you and he was a believer, then the freeing of a believing slave [is required]' (Surah An-Nisa 4:92)."
        ]
      }
    },
